From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm lanes: TF_GLM_OVN_WIN_FREE, shared rounds fill with no cost model

ai-engine a55671a7c grafted onto the pin stack. The lanes core's Model and Config gain
`free_shared`: shared windows allocate with no cost table, so windows.fill fills by
chance alone, and the config's shared table is not built. GLM's facts() sets it when
the knob is on and a drafter is loaded (`block`), so it only applies to shared rounds.
Knob off: false, the cost table and every allocation unchanged.

Pin adaptations: the source also carried shared_depth_full / shared_copy_width, which
are later-era Model fields the pin does not have, so those are left out here and ride
with their own levers; the source's shared_depth_test ref is dropped for the same
reason. free_shared_test.zig rides in this patch.

Gates on pin+0001..0015: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new.
